{title: Are You Washed in the Blood?}
{artist: Elisha A. Hoffman}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Have you been to Jesus for the [C]cleansing [G]power
Are you [D7]washed in the blood of the [G]Lamb
[G]Are you fully trusting in His [C]grace this [G]hour
Are you [D7]washed in the blood of the [G]Lamb
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Are you [G]washed in the blood
In the [C]soul-cleansing [G]blood of the [D7]Lamb
Are your [G]garments spotless? Are they [C]white as [G]snow
Are you [D7]washed in the blood of the [G]Lamb
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Are you walking daily by the [C]Saviour's [G]side
Are you [D7]washed in the blood of the [G]Lamb
[G]Do you rest each moment in the [C]Cruci[G]fied
Are you [D7]washed in the blood of the [G]Lamb
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]When the Bridegroom cometh will your [C]robes be [G]white
Pure and [D7]white in the blood of the [G]Lamb
[G]Will your soul be ready for the [C]mansions [G]bright
And be [D7]washed in the blood of the [G]Lamb
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Lay aside the garments that are [C]stained with [G]sin
And be [D7]washed in the blood of the [G]Lamb
[G]There's a fountain flowing for the [C]soul un[G]clean
O be [D7]washed in the blood of the [G]Lamb
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
